Write `buck_design(vin, vout, iout, fs, ripple_ratio=0.3, dv=0.01)` for an ideal buck converter in continuous conduction. Return `(duty, L, C)`:

- `duty` $= V_{out}/V_{in}$;
- `L` chosen so that the peak-to-peak inductor ripple is `ripple_ratio * iout`, using $\Delta I_L = (V_{in} - V_{out})D/(L f_s)$;
- `C` chosen so that the output ripple is `dv` volts, using $\Delta V = \Delta I_L/(8 f_s C)$.

The first test recovers the lesson's 10 µH and 22 µF from its ripple figures.
